{"schema":"plectis_maths_universe_excerpts_v2","paper":"erdos-1049-rational-base-lambert","excerpts":[["statement:erdos-1049-rational-base-lambert#cor:rational-base-measure","an irrationality measure uniform over\npowers","<p><em> For coprime <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>a</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span> with <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>θ</mi><mo>=</mo><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></math></span> and\nevery integer <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>r</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span>, </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></mrow></msub><mspace width=\"-0.167em\"></mspace><mrow><mo>(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>b</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mi>r</mi></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>)</mo></mrow><mo>≤</mo><mfrac><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>−</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow><mrow><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>−</mo><mi>θ</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>\n<p><em> Here <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span> is the supremum of the\nexponents <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>ν</mi></math></span> for which <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mi>ξ</mi><mo>−</mo><mi>p</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">|</mo><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mi>ν</mi></mrow></msup></math></span> has infinitely many\nreduced rational solutions. In particular, <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>μ</mi><mrow><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">i</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">r</mi></mrow></msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>31</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mi>r</mi></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>301</mn></math></span> for\nevery <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>r</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span>.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos-1049-rational-base-lambert#prop:weight-factorisation","the positive moment weights","<p><em>\nFor every <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span>, </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mn>4</mn></msup><mfrac><mrow><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></msubsup><msubsup><mi>R</mi><mi>k</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>3</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></msubsup></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>q</mi><msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mi>k</mi></msub></mrow></mfrac><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>\n<p><em>\nAt fixed <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span> these weights\nsatisfy </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span class=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><msup><mi>P</mi><mn>5</mn></msup><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"2em\"></mspace><mfrac><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><msup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mn>3</mn></msup><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>"],["statement:erdos-1049-rational-base-lambert#res:rational-base-threshold","rational-base region for Zudilin’s\nforms","<p><em> Let <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>a</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mi>b</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span> be\ncoprime integers with </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span class=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mtable displaystyle=\"true\" columnspacing=\"1em\" rowspacing=\"3pt\" data-break-align=\"middle\" minlabelspacing=\"0em\"><mtr><mtd><msup><mi>b</mi><mrow><mi>μ</mi></mrow></msup><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"2em\"></mspace><mtext>equivalently</mtext><mspace width=\"2em\"></mspace><mfrac><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>b</mi></mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mi>a</mi></mrow></mfrac><mo>&lt;</mo><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>,</mo></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>0.4056830213840605</mn><mo>…</mo><mo>,</mo></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd><mi>μ</mi><mo>=</mo><mfrac><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><msub><mi>C</mi><mn>0</mn></msub></mfrac><mo>=</mo><mn>2.4649786835749750</mn><mo>…</mo><mo>.</mo></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></span></div>\n<p><em> Then <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>a</mi><mo>/</mo><mi>b</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></math></span>\nis irrational.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos-1049-rational-base-lambert#res:sharp-fixed-base","the size of <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>N</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup></math></span> at a fixed base","<p><em> Fix <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span> and write <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>P</mi><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>;</mo><mi>q</mi><msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi></msub></math></span>, <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>/</mo><mn>6</mn></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>!</mo><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>!</mo><mo>/</mo><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>N</mi></msup></math></span>. There is a <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span> with </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>N</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>∼</mo><mi>K</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mspace width=\"0.167em\"></mspace><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><msup><mi>q</mi><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow></msup><msup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>N</mi></mrow></msup><msup><mi>N</mi><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>8</mn><mi>F</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mi>q</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow></msup><mspace width=\"2em\"></mspace><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo accent=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">→</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>"],["statement:erdos-1049-rational-base-lambert#res:thirtyone-four","","<p><em> <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>F</mi><mrow><mo minsize=\"1.2em\" maxsize=\"1.2em\">(</mo></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>31</mn><mo>/</mo><mn>4</mn><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mi>r</mi></msup><mrow><mo minsize=\"1.2em\" maxsize=\"1.2em\">)</mo></mrow></math></span> is irrational for\nevery integer <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>r</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span>.</em></p>"],["statement:erdos-1049-rational-base-lambert#res:zudilin-sharp-qorder","the first nonzero term of the Hankel\ndeterminant","<p><em> For every <span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>N</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span>,\n</em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span class=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><msub><mi>ord</mi><mi>q</mi></msub><mo>⁡</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>N</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo></mrow><mn>6</mn></mfrac><mo>,</mo></math></span></div>\n<p class=\"display-continue\"><em> and the coefficient of the first\nnonzero monomial is </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mo stretchy=\"false\">[</mo><msup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>2</mn><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>/</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">]</mo><msubsup><mi>V</mi><mi>N</mi><mo>∗</mo></msubsup><mo>=</mo><mfrac><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>!</mo><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mn>2</mn></msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>!</mo></mrow><msup><mn>2</mn><mi>N</mi></msup></mfrac><mo>.</mo></math></span></div>"],["statement:erdos-1049-rational-base-lambert#thm:geometric-moments","geometric moment determinants","<p><em> Let\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mn>0</mn><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>q</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mn>1</mn></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span> for <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span>. Suppose that, for fixed constants\n<span class=\"math inline\"><math><mi>C</mi><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><mi>κ</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></math></span>, </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span\nclass=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mtable minlabelspacing=\"0em\" displaystyle=\"true\"><mtr><mtd><mtext>(</mtext><mtext>4</mtext><mtext>)</mtext></mtd><mtd><mfrac><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mfrac><mo stretchy=\"false\">⟶</mo><mn>1</mn><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo accent=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">→</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mtext> for each fixed </mtext><mi>h</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mspace width=\"2em\"></mspace><mfrac><msub><mi>a</mi><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub></mfrac><mo>≤</mo><mi>C</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mn>1</mn><mo>+</mo><mi>h</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mi>κ</mi></msup><mspace width=\"1em\"></mspace><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>k</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>h</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>.</mo></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></span></div>\n<p><em> For <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>M</mi><mi>m</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><munder><mo>∑</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>≥</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow></munder><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><msup><mi>q</mi><mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>m</mi><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mi>k</mi></mrow></msup></math></span> and <span\nclass=\"math inline\"><math><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mo movablelimits=\"true\">det</mo><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><msub><mi>M</mi><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>+</mo><mi>j</mi></mrow></msub><msub><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>≤</mo><mi>i</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>j</mi><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>N</mi></mrow></msub></math></span>, we\nhave </em></p>\n<div class=\"math-display\"><span class=\"math display\"><math display=\"block\"><mtable minlabelspacing=\"0em\" displaystyle=\"true\"><mtr><mtd><mtext>(</mtext><mtext>5</mtext><mtext>)</mtext></mtd><mtd><msub><mi>D</mi><mi>N</mi></msub><mo>∼</mo><mrow><mi>ℳ</mi></mrow><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>q</mi><msup><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mn>3</mn></msup><msup><mi>q</mi><mrow><msub><mi>B</mi><mi>N</mi></msub></mrow></msup><msup><mi>P</mi><mrow><mn>2</mn><mi>N</mi></mrow></msup><munderover><mo>∏</mo><mrow><mi>k</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><mrow><mi>N</mi><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></munderover><msub><mi>a</mi><mi>k</mi></msub><mspace width=\"2em\"></mspace><mo stretchy=\"false\">(</mo><mi>N</mi><mo accent=\"false\" stretchy=\"false\">→</mo><mi mathvariant=\"normal\">∞</mi><mo stretchy=\"false\">)</mo><mo>.</mo></mtd></mtr></mtable></math></span></div>"]]}
